    "updated_at": "2022-01-22T23:14:41Z",
    "body": "You could probably fire up a windows 11 vm in something like vmware by enabling uefi and secure boot and install it through this method here [WSA-Script](https://github.com/LSPosed/MagiskOnWSA), this lets you install the cleanest version of wsa with gapps and magisk if you wish. \r\n\r\nThen you can just install termux via sideloading it through adb. To install cargo in termux you install the rust and rustc-dev packages. I have also found that when compiling anything with cargo on android-x86 you might have to do it a couple of times as it likes to error out a lot, even when i installed another rust package, which worked flawlessly after a couple of tries.\r\n\r\nIt appears to be an issue with starship-battery\r\nThis is what happens when i try to build starship via cargo install starship\r\n![Screenshot 2022-01-22 231151](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/25961265/150658400-9a7f2e0b-f50d-44b1-8c2f-5f13f7202bf9.png)\r\n\r\nRunning rustc --explain E043 returns this\r\n![Screenshot 2022-01-22 231312](https://user-images.githubusercontent.com/25961265/150658401-a4ef5594-49cd-47c7-97eb-fdcff1166814.png)\r\n",
    "author_association": "NONE",
